      "description": "The legacy per-case count, which the legacy resolver reads as a FLOOR (`max(legacyIterations, suite.minimumIterations)`). Stored as `runs`. Vocabulary 1 spells this field `iterations`; under `x-mcpjam-eval-vocabulary: 2` that key is the exact configured count, so the floor answers to this name (legacy spelling `runs`). NOT the same field as `iterations`: the two are never a both-spellings pair, and a PATCH that names neither leaves the stored floor exactly as it was."
